<p>That ending note just wrecks this. If you've done your job well here (and I would say that up to this point you have), it should be pretty obvious that a weird metal construct sporting pieces of your former co-worker would be fucking disturbing. Having it spelled out explicitly, in the context of the endless and mostly pointless squabbles about object class no less, pulls the rug out from under me as a reader. Instead of finishing and going &quot;hmm, yeah, that would be pretty fucked up&quot; as I think about, I get Site Director McAuthor jabbing me in the ribs going &quot;yeah, pretty scary, huh? Just wanted to make sure you got the point!&quot;</p>

