			<div class="content" id="post-content-2474625">
									

<p>Seconded; what it adds to me is the human element colliding with the dispassionate detachment the Foundation requires. They could destroy this thing easily- it's just metal and flesh. They aren't protecting the world from this thing. They're protecting this thing from every sane person's first though: kill the monster.</p>
<p>The bigger thing is that he was apparently sufficiently okay with the body-part stealing monstrosity prior to the incident&#8230; but when his colleague dies, now its not just a bunch of body parts. Its part of a person he had conversations with, someone with a name. That memo is the evidence of Dr. G loosing his faith in the Foundation's basic philosophy; the idea that they can both allow something like this to live <em>and</em> still have a regard for human life.</p>

